# Local agent / editor config — machine-specific, not part of the app.
/.claude
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# OS droppings. Developed on Windows, deployed to a static host, so both
# families turn up in a working tree at some point.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Node. Only ever used for tooling — `npm test` and `npm run icons` — and
# package.json has no dependencies key, so node_modules/ should not exist at
# all. Ignored anyway: the day someone runs `npm i something` to try an idea,
# this is what stops 30,000 files landing in a diff.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.log

# Secrets. Defensive: there are none today and the design has nowhere to put
# one — no backend, no accounts, no API keys, and js/config.js ships empty
# strings. A static site that needed a secret would be a static site with a
# secret published to the world, so if one of these ever appears here it is a
# mistake, and it should be a mistake that cannot be committed.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# NOT ignored, on purpose: icons/*.png.
#
# They are generated by `npm run icons`, which normally means "don't commit the
# output" — but there is no build step here and nothing runs on the host. GitHub
# Pages serves this directory verbatim, and manifest.webmanifest points at those
# exact files, so an icons/ that only exists on a developer's machine is a PWA
# that cannot be installed. They are committed artefacts, like index.html.
